  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "On the Jia clan caravan treehouse’s third floor on Qing Mao Mountain, Gu Yue Yao Ji names the glowing sphere for her granddaughter as a white silver Relic Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          111
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_jia_family",
          "loc_qing_mao_mountain",
          "char_gu_yue_yao_ji"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan later buys and uses one of his own in Shang clan city.",
        "chapters": [
          296
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "loc_shang_clan_city"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan recalls that after Ma Hong Yun left slave status and hunted poorly as a mortal, he smashed a rock in anger and found a white silver Relic Gu under it. He contributed the Gu to Ma tribe’s young tribe leader, who needed it, rewarded him, and gave him a chance to awaken and cultivate.",
        "chapters": [
          441
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "ma-hong-yuns-find",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_ma_hong_yun",
          "fac_ma_tribe"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Later text calls Relic Gu a sphere-shaped mortal Gu, thumb-sized, with an ordinary appearance, and names rank three white silver Relic Gu in the same rank list, with mortal-market value around fifty thousand primeval stones. Relic Gu at rank one to three sell in batches in treasure yellow heaven. Relic Gu can only form naturally; Gu Immortals, including those of Lang Ya blessed land and Heavenly Court, cannot create them, because they are human path Gu worms that form more readily where many humans or variant humans live.",
        "chapters": [
          1796
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "human-path-form",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_immortal",
          "loc_lang_ya_blessed_land",
          "fac_heavenly_court",
          "sys_gu_worms"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
